- In cases of asynchronous IO, it is not always safe to immediately call `fput(file)` in the error path or at function exit, especially **if an asynchronous event might race and need the file reference after this function returns**.
- According to the vulnerability knowledge, this premature release was the root cause of a use-after-free.
