- `cleanup_async_copy(copy)` is always called unconditionally, at the end, outside of branches—this matches the fix behavior, not the buggy one.
- The resources cleaned up *within* the branches are either file handles (with `nfsd4_cleanup_inter_ssc` or `nfsd4_cleanup_intra_ssc`), which only clean up if the handles were validly opened.
